# Skill installer artifact. Kept on disk on purpose: it carries 7 files the installed
# copy at ~/.claude/skills/living-systems-ui does not have. Not deleted, not committed.
living-systems-ui.zip

# Generated evidence bundle for a research dispatch: a concatenation of files that already
# live in this repo, so committing it would ship a copy that is stale on the next edit.
# Rebuild with scripts/build_r8_pack.py.
docs/research/R8-evidence-pack.md

# Same rule as the R8 pack: a generated concatenation of files that already live here.
# Rebuild with scripts/build_r13_pack.py.
docs/research/R13-evidence-pack.md

# Generated evidence bundle for R14. Rebuild with scripts/build_r14_pack.py.
docs/research/R14-evidence-pack.md

# Generated evidence bundle for R16. Rebuild with scripts/build_r16_pack.py.
docs/research/R16-evidence-pack.md

# Live Power BI capture for a named client: workspace and model names for a production
# tenant, plus measured sales, cost and conversion rows. LOCAL_ONLY, unconditionally —
# the DAX result rows are the client's commercial data. Kept on disk as authoritative
# evidence for the PBI verification, ignored so no `git add -A` can stage it.
docs/evidence/marketing-model-v1/pbi-ad-sales-live-2026-09-01/

# Generated review pack for external architecture review. 3.4 MB, and it carries the
# client-identifying content AF-RELEASE-GATE-01 §4.1 enumerates — so it must never be staged into
# a repository whose remote is public. `docs/release-gate/AF-RELEASE-GATE-01-2026-09-01.md` §5
# item 6 records the same hazard for the live PBI capture and calls it "a live hazard, not a
# hypothetical" because five sessions share this checkout. Rebuild from docs/_index/ at any time.
agent-factory-research-review-pack.zip

# Generated architecture-review supplement, 2026-09-02. Same hazard, same remedy as the review
# pack above: it bundles docs/_index/corpus_manifest.yaml, document_catalog.md, concept_index.yaml,
# current_vs_proposed.md, high_leverage_concepts.md, research_gap_candidates.md and
# docs/research/backlog.yaml, and a leak sweep over exactly these 15 entries returned client
# identifiers in all seven of them (two client/brand names and two ticket keys, ~30 occurrences)
# original pass, not introduced by the supplement. The remote is public and five sessions share
# this checkout, so one `git add -A` is the whole failure mode. Rebuild deterministically at any
# time: python scripts/build_supplement_zip.py
agent-factory-architecture-supplement.zip

# Claude Design export of the CELL OS avatar system, 105.3 MB — over GitHub's hard 100 MB
# per-file limit, so any commit containing it makes the push to the public `personal` remote
# unpushable and only history surgery removes it. Kept on disk; re-export from Claude Design.
docs/design/claude-design/*.zip
